        "original_id": "f8279934-4299-5c47-bd5b-f4e736fdf528",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hermann Neubacher\n- Places: Balkans, Greece, Serbia, Albania, Montenegro\n- Organizations: German Foreign Ministry, Kingdom of Italy, Allied armed forces\n- Political Entities: Albanian Kingdom (1943–44)\n- Events: Second World War, Armistice of 8 September 1943\n\nFacts:\n- During the Second World War, Hermann Neubacher was appointed the leading German Foreign Ministry official for the Balkans, including Greece, Serbia, Albania, and Montenegro.\n- Before the armistice between Italy and the Allied armed forces on 8 September 1943, Albania was in a de jure personal union with the Kingdom of Italy and was de facto under Italian control.\n- Between 1943 and 1944, the Albanian Kingdom existed as a de jure independent country.",
